JDBC is java api to connect and execute queries with database.
it is also called as thin driver.

types of jdbc drivers:
*jdbc-odbc bridge driver
*native driver
*network protocol driver
*thin driver

Java database connectivity:
1)Register driver
2)Create connection
3)Create statement
4)Execute queries
5)Close connection

JDBC Methods:
prepareStatement()	- prepares an SQl query
setInt()	- sets an integer value
setString()	- sets an string value
setLong()	- sets an long value
executeUpdate()	- executes INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE
executeQuery()	- executes SELECT
ResultSet	- holds the retrieved records
rs.next()	- moves to the next record


